{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) meaningfully outperforms single-modality baselines, and which moderate-complexity multimodal setup provides a strong reference point. config_008 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat fusion) tests this core hypothesis with a balanced architecture: pca_n2000 gives a solid 2000-dim RNA representation, resnet50 is a proven but not the most expensive image encoder, and concat fusion is a straightforward combination strategy. It avoids the added cost of multiprofile aggregation and ViT-L, keeping training time moderate (estimated ~middle of the cost range, roughly 1.5–2x a single-modality run). If it performs well, I can exploit by adding multiprofile, upgrading to ViT-L, or testing transformer aggregation in subsequent experiments. If it underperforms, I learn early that the multimodal pipeline needs different encoders or fusion, saving budget. This is the best use of experiment 1: it directly addresses the highest-impact design question (does multimodal help?) at moderate cost, establishing a strong anchor for the remaining 9 experiments."
}

